== 5.6 Chapter 5 in the Exam Hall — a Two-Minute Set

#mcq(1, [The students worked \_\_\_ and passed the examination \_\_\_], [hard / easy], [hardly / easily], [hard / easily], [hardly / easy])
#mcq(2, [Of the two brothers, Chidi is the \_\_\_], [tallest], [most tall], [taller], [more taller])
#mcq(3, [Choose the sentence that is correctly written.], [Having eaten the meal, the plates were washed.], [Having eaten the meal, she washed the plates.], [Having eaten the meal, it was time to wash plates.], [Having eaten the meal, the plates were washed by her.])
#mcq(4, [The success of the project depends \_\_\_ the cooperation of the community.], [of], [on], [to], [for])

#answer-key-grid(("C", "C", "B", "B"))

#answer-notes((
  ("C", [worked needs the adverb hard, which means with effort, and passed needs easily. Hardly means almost not, and easy is an adjective.]),
  ("C", [two brothers means a comparison of two, so the comparative taller is right. Tallest and most tall would need three or more, and more taller doubles the comparison.]),
  ("B", [the opening participial phrase must be followed by the person who ate. Only she can have eaten the meal, so only B is correct.]),
  ("B", [depend on is a fixed pair. Of, to and for do not collocate with depend in this sense, however natural they may sound in translation.]),
))

